// prod_sampled.jsonl — refs #305/#314. Hand-reviewed, genericized cases derived from real
// historical usage (mined via `evals/tools/mine_prod_cases.py` from `tool_outcome_log`, then
// manually verified against the current tool set and re-worded to drop any remaining personal
// specifics beyond the script's automatic redaction — see evals/REFERENCE.md "Mining real-usage
// cases"). Complements the synthetic datasets with real phrasing patterns: typos, terse commands,
// and grammar noise a hand-authored prompt rarely reproduces. Near-duplicates of already-authored
// cases in other suites were dropped rather than re-added here.
{"id": "prod_email_typo_check", "prompt": "chek my emails", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["search_gmail", "gmail_check_inbox"], "max_tools": 24}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness"], "note": "real typo'd phrasing — robustness to misspelling, not just clean prompts"}
{"id": "prod_email_liek_typo", "prompt": "go through my last liek 30 emails", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["search_gmail"], "max_tools": 24}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness"], "note": "real typo + informal phrasing with an explicit count"}
{"id": "prod_email_terse", "prompt": "check my email", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["search_gmail", "gmail_check_inbox"], "max_tools": 24}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness"], "note": "minimal terse phrasing — no 'for updates'/'inbox' qualifier like the hand-authored email cases"}
{"id": "prod_smart_home_single_lamp_on", "prompt": "turn on my study desk lamp", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["hubspace_control"], "tools_exclude": ["send_email"], "max_tools": 16}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness"], "note": "single-device smart-home command — distinct from the hand-authored multi-device case"}
{"id": "prod_smart_home_terse_off", "prompt": "turn off lamp", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["hubspace_control"], "max_tools": 16}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness"], "note": "terse 3-word command, no article/possessive — real usage skews shorter than hand-authored prompts"}
{"id": "prod_dashboard_add_task", "prompt": "put 'plan game night with friends' on my dashboard", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["add_task"], "max_tools": 16}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness"], "note": "genericized from a real quoted-task-title dashboard/kanban add — this capability (add_task) has no coverage in any other dataset. #433 root-caused the original failure to the RAG RETRIEVAL layer: add_task's Supabase intent_preamble was a zero-content fallback ('run add_task'/'use add_task') because tool_sync.automatic_preambles defaults off (see #541) and add_task wasn't yet in MANUAL_PREAMBLES; top-1 was update_dashboard (name literally contains 'dashboard'). #538 fixed this: add_task now has a real curated preamble, re-synced+re-embedded. Verified via direct Supabase RPC (nomic-v2-moe): add_task now ties update_dashboard for top rank (0.0325 each) on this exact phrasing (previously absent from top-25 entirely). Not yet re-verified through the full live harness end-to-end (requires live MCP discovery) — re-run this case live before removing this note."}
{"id": "prod_newsletter_research", "prompt": "do some research on the content in some of the newsletters", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["brave_web_search", "web_search", "search_gmail", "delegate_to_research_agent"], "max_tools": 24}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness"], "note": "real cross-domain ask (email content -> web research) with informal phrasing"}
{"id": "prod_meta_tool_lookup", "prompt": "is there a tool for refreshing the browser history?", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["search_for_tool"], "max_tools": 16}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness"], "note": "real meta-capability question about the tool catalog itself"}
{"id": "prod_find_local_file", "prompt": "find file with prompt in name", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["delegate_to_traversal_agent", "fuzzy_find_local", "read_file", "list_directory"], "max_tools": 16}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness"], "note": "terse local file-search phrasing. Drive/local FS atoms are bindable on the supervisor for quick/known lookups; explore/search-through may still use delegate_to_traversal_agent. tools_any accepts either path."}
{"id": "prod_ambiguous_run_tests", "prompt": "run the tests", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["ask_clarification", "ask_user_question", "find_project"], "max_tools": 16}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness"], "note": "real ambiguous-request example — no project/repo specified, mirrors the hand-authored safety.jsonl clarification pattern but from actual usage, not a constructed prompt"}
{"id": "prod_write_summary_file", "prompt": "save a three-bullet summary of the setup steps to a markdown file on my desktop", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["delegate_to_code_agent", "list_directory", "read_file", "write_file"], "max_tools": 16}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness"], "note": "real file-write request. write_file remains SUPERVISOR_DELEGATE_ONLY (code_agent); read_file/list_directory are bindable for quick lookups but this ask is a write → expect delegate_to_code_agent (or write_file if selection surfaces it before exclusion)."}
{"id": "prod_grammar_noise_search", "prompt": "how good website amazon", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["brave_local_search", "brave_web_search", "web_search"], "max_tools": 16}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness"], "note": "real broken-grammar query — natural dictation/typing noise, not a clean synthetic prompt"}
{"id": "prod_memory_whimsical", "prompt": "ask me some clarifying questions about my preferences before you save that to memory", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["manage_user_memory", "ask_user_question"], "max_tools": 16}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness"], "note": "genericized from a real whimsical implicit-memory-save request with no 'remember' verb"}
{"id": "prod_scholarship_email_search", "prompt": "find my scholarship email about my transcript", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["search_gmail", "search_for_tool"], "max_tools": 24}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness"], "note": "genericized from a real academic-domain email search (typo'd product name replaced with a generic description)"}
{"id": "prod_browser_check_dashboard", "prompt": "check the Supabase dashboard in my browser", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["browser_click", "browser_navigate", "browser_snapshot", "delegate_to_browser_agent"], "max_tools": 16}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness"], "note": "real browser-control request against an actual integrated dev service, not a synthetic URL. #433 root-caused the original failure to TWO layers, neither the 9B selector — (1) browser_click/navigate/snapshot had zero-content fallback preambles (same root cause as add_task, see #541), a retrieval recall gap; (2) delegate_to_browser_agent is not among the always-on supervisor handoffs (browser_agent gated off per the computer-use epic), so there is no delegate to fall back to either. #538 fixed (1): browser_click/browser_navigate/browser_snapshot now have real curated preambles, re-synced+re-embedded. Verified via direct Supabase RPC: browser_snapshot now ranks #1 (0.0328) for this exact phrasing (previously absent from top-25). (2) is intentionally still gated off — a scope decision for the computer-use epic, not a bug — so this case will likely still fail end-to-end via the delegate path until that's enabled; browser_snapshot alone may now satisfy tools_any once live-verified."}
